bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_input_button_label_width_not_device_shaped_2026-11-28, 0, "form_control_label_width_milli_px now shapes a <button> label at the device font size at k > 1 (13.3333 px x k, LayoutUnit of a device px). The label of <input type=button|submit|reset> does not go through that function for its width, so its box at k > 1 is still k x the k = 1 width. Chrome 159 sizes both the same way. Not measured in Chrome yet for the input case: expected the same sub-device-px difference as <button> (Forms & Media: 361.53 device px vs 4 x 90.3594 = 361.44)."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_input_button_label_width_not_device_shaped_2026-11-28, P3, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "web render: <input type=button/submit> label width is k x the 1x width at k>1 while <button> is shaped at the device font size", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_foundation.spl, 1004, "<input type=submit value='Forms &amp; Media'> beside <button>Forms &amp; Media</button> at device scale 4; compare box widths with Chrome 159", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_input_button_label_width_not_device_shaped_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 tabbar lane: forms-media 4x frame is byte-identical before and after 35d45555c32, so the catalog does not show the difference. Needs a Chrome-measured spec before changing the input path."
    web_render_input_button_label_width_not_device_shaped_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 button-label-cluster lane: measured. Chrome 159: <input type=submit value='Forms &amp; Media'> 108.3594 (k=1) / 108.3828 (k=4), the input's own box already matched on base. Red in what FOLLOWS it: k=1 the next button's label ink started at 118 (Chrome 119) and the reset label after <input type=button> at 99 (Chrome 100) -- inline_item_width_err_milli had no input-button branch, so the pen after it was whole px; k=4 the following button's right border was 864 (Chrome 863) -- the pen came from the input's device-snapped width and the button's right edge from its snapped left + rounded width. Fix: inline_item_width_err_milli_with_lead gains an input-button branch (label LayoutUnit, device-shaped at k>1; helpers input_button_label_text / input_button_label_exact_milli in layout_text.spl), and the inline loop re-snaps an auto-width button / input-button right edge to round(k x exact right) (inline_control_device_delta_milli). Red->green: test/01_unit/browser_engine/button_input_device_width_chrome159_spec.spl AC-2."

